/*Q29.
In a small school, the teachers are adopting a new grading system to evaluate students' performance. Each student receives a score, and the school wants to convert these scores into grades. The grading system is as follows:
  - A: 90-100 (inclusive)
  - B: 75-89 (inclusive)
  - C: 60-74 (inclusive)
  - D: 45-59 (inclusive)
  - F: Below 45

Write a Java program to help the school convert the scores into grades.

Input Format:
  - The first line is an integer representing the score of a student.

Output Format:
  - The output is a character representing the corresponding grade.*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Descending threshold checks cover every integer with no gaps.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int score = sc.nextInt();

        char grade;
        if (score >= 90) {
            grade = 'A';
        } else if (score >= 75) {
            grade = 'B';
        } else if (score >= 60) {
            grade = 'C';
        } else if (score >= 45) {
            grade = 'D';
        } else {
            grade = 'F';
        }
        System.out.println(grade);
        sc.close();
    }
}

